					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 4: LINEAR INTERPOLATION BETWEEN POINTS (ADVANCED)\n\nIn this example we are using the crossfader to interpolate between points.\nWe start with a Circle Pattern, giving us our Float2 points.\nTo draw the pattern, we use the Line node.\nThe collection is shifted by 1 to get the end points of the line.\n\nNext we use the CrossFader at 50% to interpolate between the shifted collection and the original.\nThese points are drawn from 0,0 to the interpolated points."
					}
				},
